sequenceDiagram
    participant Scheduler as Background Scheduler
    participant ExpiryJob as IdentifierExpirationJob
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Log as ECS JSON log

    Note over Scheduler: Daily at a randomised time 03:45–05:45 local<br/>(load spread across EU gates). Configurable via IDENTIFIER_EXPIRY_CRON.

    Scheduler->>+ExpiryJob: triggerExpiryJob()

    ExpiryJob->>+DB: SELECT DISTINCT ON (dataset_id) *<br/>FROM consignments<br/>ORDER BY dataset_id, created_at DESC<br/>(filter: status='active' AND mode='road'<br/> AND transport_date + INTERVAL '14 days' < NOW())
    Note over DB: Uses idx_consignments_dataset_latest +<br/>idx_consignments_status_active partial index.<br/>Cabotage retention per Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4).
    DB-->>-ExpiryJob: [550e8400-…, a1b2c3d4-…, c3d4e5f6-…] (latest rows)

    loop For each expired road consignment
        ExpiryJob->>+DB: INSERT INTO consignments<br/>(dataset_id, platform_id, gate_id, xml,<br/>status, mode, vehicle_plate, …,<br/>transport_date, expires_at, created_at)<br/>VALUES (… same as latest row, but status='inactive')
        DB-->>-ExpiryJob: new row inserted
        Note over DB: No UPDATE — append-only. The newly-inserted<br/>row becomes the latest for this dataset_id;<br/>reads picking DISTINCT ON now see status='inactive'.
        ExpiryJob->>Log: { event.action: "identifier.expire",<br/>efti.dataset.id: "550e8400-…", efti.expiry.reason: "cabotage_14d" }
    end

    ExpiryJob->>+DB: INSERT INTO jobs_execution_log<br/>(job_name, started_at, finished_at, status, details)<br/>VALUES ('expiry-job', $start, NOW(), 'completed',<br/>jsonb_build_object('expired_count', 3))
    DB-->>-ExpiryJob: ok
    ExpiryJob-->>-Scheduler: done

    Note over Scheduler: Non-road modes (maritime/rail/air/multimodal)<br/>are NOT expired by this job — Reg 2024/1942 Art 11(4)<br/>cabotage retention applies to road only.<br/>Old (non-latest) consignments rows are archived<br/>nightly by CronManager (Epic 26).
